---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Sam — Sam's Menswear · Vaughan"
  description="Sam is a personal master tailor in Vaughan — over two decades cutting suits by hand for the men of Vaughan, Thornhill and Toronto. Never outsourced, never rushed."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div data-reveal>
        <div class="eyebrow-rule">The Tailor</div>
        <h1>One man, <em>one tape,</em> one notebook.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Sam has been measuring shoulders and marking chalk for the men of Vaughan and Thornhill for over twenty years. Every garment is drawn, cut and fitted personally — never outsourced, never rushed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split wide-left" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <h2 class="h-2" style="text-transform: uppercase;">The work begins the <em style="font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; text-transform: none; color: var(--oxblood);">same way, every time.</em></h2>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 24px;">
            A measuring tape. A pencil. A long conversation about the man inside the cloth. Whether you're standing at the altar, walking into a boardroom, or fitting a son for his first suit, Sam starts by learning how you actually move, sit and stand — then draws a pattern that belongs to you alone.
          </p>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 18px;">
            There is no back room of subcontractors here, no sizes graded from a template. Sam cuts what Sam sells. The pattern he drafts on your first visit is kept — in pencil, in a notebook — and every jacket, trouser and shirt you commission for years afterward begins from it.
          </p>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 18px;">
            It is, deliberately, a slow way to work. It is also the only way he has ever found to make a garment that outlives the occasion it was made for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; background: var(--paper-cream); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 28px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;">
            <div class="crop-marks"></div>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 260 320" style="width:100%; height:100%; display:block;" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
              <g fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <!-- shears -->
                <circle cx="70" cy="240" r="16"/>
                <circle cx="104" cy="240" r="16"/>
                <path d="M82 228 L 200 96"/>
                <path d="M96 232 L 214 100"/>
                <path d="M200 96 L 214 100"/>
                <!-- measuring tape curl -->
                <path d="M40 70 C 100 40, 160 100, 210 60" stroke-width="6" stroke="var(--gold)" opacity="0.65"/>
                <path d="M40 70 C 100 40, 160 100, 210 60" stroke-width="1" stroke="var(--ink)" opacity="0.5"/>
                <!-- pencil -->
                <path d="M60 150 L 150 190"/>
                <path d="M60 150 L 52 156 L 60 162 Z" fill="var(--oxblood)" stroke="none"/>
              </g>
              <g font-family="Cormorant Garamond" font-style="italic" font-size="12" fill="var(--ink-mute)" letter-spacing="2">
                <text x="130" y="300" text-anchor="middle">Measured personally.</text>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Values -->
  <section class="section"
           style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent 0%, var(--paper-cream) 50%, transparent 100%);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="chapter-no">No. 02</div>
        <h2 class="h-1" style="text-transform: uppercase; max-width: 18ch;">How Sam <em>works.</em></h2>
        <div class="right">A few fixed principles</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid cols-3" data-reveal-stagger>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ I</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Cut by hand, by Sam</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Your measurements are taken, your pattern drafted, and your cloth cut by the same pair of hands. Nothing is sent out. Nothing is graded from a size.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ II</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">One client at a time</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Appointments are private. The atelier is a quiet room of wool and light — so a fitting has the unhurried feel of an old tailor's workshop, because that's what it is.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ III</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">The pattern is kept</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Your first visit earns a pattern that stays on file. The next shirt, the next suit, your son's first jacket — each one begins where the last left off.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ IV</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">A family business</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">Sam — or a member of the family — will sit with you for the conversation, remember your shoulders, and pick up the phone when you call.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ V</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Closed for Shabbos</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">The atelier is closed all Shabbos, Yom Tov and chol hamoed. Fridays we close two hours before sundown so the family can prepare. Some things come before the work.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="feature-num">№ VI</div>
          <h3 class="h-3">Honest before the cloth is cut</h3>
          <p class="body-prose" style="margin-top: 12px;">The first consultation costs nothing and carries no obligation. If we work together, the garment is quoted honestly before a single thread is committed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pull quote -->
  <section class="section tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div data-reveal style="max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center;">
        <span class="quote__mark" style="position: static; display: block; text-align: center;">“</span>
        <p class="quote__text" style="font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px); text-align: center;">My father bought his Shabbos suit here in 1996. I bought my son's bar mitzvah suit here last winter. Some things you don't change.</p>
        <div class="quote__attr" style="margin-top: 20px;">A. Rosenberg · Vaughan</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section flush">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="booking-block" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow-rule" style="color: var(--gold-soft); margin-bottom: 28px;">
            <span style="background: var(--navy-deep);">Come sit with Sam</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="h-1">Begin with a <em>conversation.</em></h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 24px;">The first fitting is unhurried, candid and obligation-free. Bring a jacket you love — or one you don't.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
          <a href="/book" class="btn is-primary" data-open-booking data-no-transition>Book a Fitting</a>
          <div class="contact-tag" style="margin-top: 12px;">
            Or call directly
            <div class="num">647 · 458 · 0711</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
